{"timestamp":"2026-09-20T06:03:24.215Z","ordinal":65,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0bd69-84b7-74c2-a5d3-23e6bb426a26","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<user_action>\n  <context>User initiated a review task. Here's the full review output from reviewer model. User may select one or more comments to resolve.</context>\n  <action>review</action>\n  <results>\n  The patch introduces a failing test and correctness issues in review generation, writing tools, and mobile presentation. Typecheck and client build passed; the full test suite reported 1,466 passes, 39 skips, and one failure. Browser tests could not start because the configured dev server exited.\n\nFull review comments:\n\n- [P2] Update the settings wiring test for the new dropdowns — /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/routes/settings/index.tsx:1870-1872\n  Adding these five dropdowns leaves `settings-select-wiring.test.ts:13` expecting exactly 11 `SiteSelect` instances, while the page now contains 16. Consequently, `bun run test` fails. Update the assertion alongside these controls, preferably checking their identities rather than a brittle total.\n\n- [P2] Remove fictitious judge metrics from judgement-only reviews — /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/rubric/rubric-panel.tsx:733-739\n  For a successful Jev pass, `result.judges` is empty, so `combineJudgesAndStatic()` supplies default judge mean and minimum scores of 5. The existing review prompt presents both as actual judge scores and requests reconciliation with the static score. Adding this disclaimer leaves contradictory evidence in the request. Use a judgement-specific payload and prompt that omit nonexistent persona scores.\n\n- [P2] Start the drag tests inside the selected text — /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/e2e/drag-selection.e2e.ts:140-144\n  The paragraph bounding box spans the manuscript width, but the selected `Beta paragraph.` occupies only its leftmost portion. Starting at the box's horizontal midpoint presses outside the selection, collapsing it instead of starting a native text drag. The caret test repeats this mistake. Derive the starting coordinates from the selected text range rather than the block rectangle.\n\n- [P2] Preserve the mobile breakpoint hiding tour hotspots — /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/global.css:2633-2639\n  This unlayered `display: flex` overrides Tailwind's layered `hidden` utility on the tour buttons. Consequently, the desktop-positioned hotspots remain visible below `lg`, including on phones where the sidebar elements they describe are hidden. They instead overlay unrelated manuscript content. Put the display rule behind the desktop breakpoint or in an appropriate cascade layer.\n\n- [P2] Include the selected focus in the circling check — /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/writing-lenses.ts:510-512\n  The circling UI offers a passage or question to focus on, and `inputs()` includes that value, but this request sends only revisions and its instructions never reference the focus. Entering a specific passage therefore produces the same request as leaving the field empty. Include the bounded focus in the request and instructions, or remove the unsupported control.\n  </results>\n  </user_action>\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0bd63-0c37-7e41-a9c4-ea932a30722b","create_time":1789884204.215218,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}}}
