{"timestamp":"2026-09-20T06:03:51.107Z","ordinal":94,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0bd69-edc2-78f2-a903-5f109d0530d2","call_id":"call_6CTn2RzcaE7MJc4fpREM34Tf","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"6f66b7\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004768,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3805,\"output\":\"# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating Jev/model-cascade shared judgement foundation\\nscope: Continue the shared cross-surface judgement foundation while completing the still-unreplaced judge sites, telemetry, evolution wiring, and full validation.\\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating; reuse_rule=reinspect the heavily dirty branch and targeted diffs; treat the shared contracts as partial implementation, not completion of docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md.\\n\\n## Task 1: Add typed Jev/model-cascade contracts and pure decision helpers, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; foundation implemented, post-boosting full suite not rerun)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Jev, TypeSafe, System One, JudgementCaller, learner-contracts, cascade-router, MiniCPM5, Needle, evidence-by-selection, assessment, retrieval, boosting\\n\\n## Task 2: Replace all LLM-as-judge paths and finish cascade phases, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/keating, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4, partial; all three delegated workers hit usage limits)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- benchmark_judge.py, export-judge.ts, trajectory-passes.ts, model-adapters.ts, policy-judgement.ts, mastery.ts, learner-state.ts, runtime_or_model_changed, telemetry, injection tests\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when the user required “do it all end to end” and “Full replacement everywhere” -> continue through all planned judge sites; do not present the contract layer as sufficient completion [Task 1][Task 2]\\n- when the user required a local judgement model “separate model configurable in settings” -> keep tutor-model and judgement-model settings independent [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- The shared cross-platform location is `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/`: `contracts.ts`, `projections.ts`, `router.ts`, `wire.ts`, `system-one.ts`, `local-backend.ts`, `assessment.ts`, `retrieval.ts`, and `boosting.ts`, exported through the package root. CLI, web, and mobile already consume `@keating/learner-contracts`. [Task 1]\\n- Cascade routing starts at the cheapest tier, escalates only residue, skips uncalibrated tiers, never falls back from a pinned backend, and returns deterministic baseline plus abstention when exhausted. Thresholds key on backend/model/calibration/question digest. [Task 1]\\n- Hosted System One is `POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone`; Choice is a criteria map, Score an ordered criteria array, and Noul has no confidence. Do not surface upstream bodies; same-origin gateway calls omit credentials. [Task 1]\\n- `web/src/keating/judgement-model.ts` stores the independent `off|local|hosted` setting, defaults local to `RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX`, and accepts only same-origin gateway paths. Local Needle answers are typed/closed-vocabulary and omit unanswerable questions. [Task 1]\\n- Assessment helpers keep readiness Nouls one-directional, use per-item performance Nouls, bucket duration/due dates, and mark uncertain open answers `grading: \\\"pending\\\"`. Retrieval uses calibrated z-scores, exact learner-message evidence, observed confidence <=0.65, and a 128-fact cap. Start boosting with a depth-limited tree and deterministic held-out rows. [Task 1]\\n- The remaining plan targets include `scripts/training/benchmark_judge.py`, `web/src/keating/export-judge.ts`, `web/src/keating/trajectory-passes.ts`, `shared/evolution/model-adapters.ts`, `src/core/policy-judgement.ts`, `src/core/mastery.ts`, and `src/core/learner-state.ts`. Preserve server-side-only TypeSafe credentials, `NEEDLE_TELEMETRY=0`, `DO_NOT_TRACK=1`, evidence taxonomy, and no automatic irreversible action from judgement alone. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Bun tests can pass while a type-only import is wrong because imports are stripped. After tests, always run `bun run typecheck`; assessment types belong in `contracts.ts`, not `projections.ts`. [Task 1]\\n- Symptom: `ReferenceError: localStorage is not defined` in web setting tests -> use the existing inline storage/window/custom-event shim pattern in `web/src/test/learner-context.test.ts`. [Task 1]\\n- The recorded `187 pass / 0 fail` package result and typecheck predate later boosting changes. Rerun the entire package suite before calling it green. For web: `cd web && bun run panda`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`, then `bun test`; also run root/Bun, benchmark, evidence-integrity, cache-key, offline/no-network, and injection checks. [Task 1][Task 2]\\n- All three workers terminated with usage-limit errors and delivered no implementation result. Continue directly or use smaller bounded tasks; do not assume their files changed. [Task 2]\\n\\n# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook native terminal UI Canvas parity and Jev review\\nscope: Continue native OpenTUI/Canvas parity and targeted UX refinement with modular TUI seams, verified local behavior, and an honest boundary around the blocked second Jev review.\\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook; reuse_rule=reuse the module/layout and OpenTUI behavior findings after checking the current TUI API and worktree; do not infer a second external review or new tests from this rollout.\\n\\n## Task 1: Implement Canvas parity in the native TUI, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; implementation and local verification succeeded, new tests intentionally deferred)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- textbook, native-tui, canvas, OpenTUI, src/tui, src/themes.ts, renderer.keyInput, destroyRecursively, VHS, similarity-ts\\n\\n## Task 2: Apply Jev terminal UX review refinements, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/textbook, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-19T05:08:40+00:00, thread_id=01a0b98d-1314-74b3-b9ff-f31175a6e455, partial; first external review plus local follow-up, second review blocked)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Jev, TypeSafe, systemone, search_typing_safe, borderless inspector, footer scanability, auto-mode classifier, skate typesafe_api_key@secrets\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when scoping implementation, the user said \\\"use your best judgement tbh\\\" after rejecting repeated questions -> decide a reasonable product scope and proceed rather than asking more product questions. [Task 1]\\n- when asked for Canvas parity, the user said \\\"Don't write tests right now, just focus on implementation\\\" -> do not add new tests until that boundary is re-enabled; retain existing tests as evidence only. [Task 1]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- The native TUI is modular under `src/tui/{index,state,keymap,focus,preview,sidebar,panel}.ts`; `src/app.ts` is a compatibility re-export, and `src/themes.ts` is the shared Canvas/TUI palette and chrome source consumed by `src/web/html.ts`. Generation guards plus `destroyRecursively()` prevent stale asynchronous story renderables and leaks. [Task 1]\\n- In this OpenTUI version, use `renderer.keyInput.on(\\\"keypress\\\", ...)`; `renderer.on(\\\"keypress\\\")` is a no-op. `InputRenderableOptions` excludes `height`, so collapse its wrapping `BoxRenderable`; omit `borderColor` entirely when `border: false`, because supplying it forces a border. [Task 1]\\n- Verified locally: `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, `bun test` 36 pass/0 fail, VHS showed search/navigation/sidebar/inspector/theme/viewport/footer behavior, and `similarity-ts src/tui src/themes.ts` found no duplicate functions or similar types. [Task 1]\\n- Search-mode safety was checked mechanically by enumerating printable characters through `resolveAction(..., \\\"search\\\")`; none are intercepted. Apply the evidence rather than trusting Jev's lower `search_typing_safe` score. [Task 2]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- VHS reports `Module not found \\\"dist/index.js\\\"` from a scratchpad -> put an explicit `cd /home/diogenes/Projects/textbook` inside the tape and use relative output filenames; an apparent `>` artifact can be the VHS shell prompt, not a TUI scrollbar defect. [Task 1]\\n- The second Jev submission was blocked by the auto-mode classifier -> do not bypass it; retain the first HTTP-200 review and local checks as the available external-review evidence. Never print or persist the Skate-provided TypeSafe credential. [Task 2]\\n\\n# Task Group: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne Jev provider, rubric, and writing tools\\nscope: Route typed Jev judgements through Not Organic, maintain Jev-first rubric and optional writing lenses, and distinguish local implementation from verified provider production.\\napplies_to: cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne plus /home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider; reuse_rule=reinspect both dirty worktrees and deploy state; direct TypeSafe use is local-only when Not Organic is enabled.\\n\\n## Task 1: Stage then complete the Not Organic Jev provider boundary, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; source changes uncommitted and undeployed)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; staged gateway work preceded guarded completion)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- Jev, TypeSafe, Not Organic, POST /v1/judgement, judgement:evaluate, DPoP, GatewayConfig.typesafe, TYPESAFE_API_KEY, ProviderStore, reserve dispatch accept settle\\n\\n## Task 2: Use Jev-first rubric scoring with safe fallback, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; final checks intentionally omitted)\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-09-28-01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:37:12+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6c8-324a-7d60-a2fa-a16f00cc5a18, partial; earlier 1104-test evidence)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- runRubricPass, judgementRubricResult, rubric-grade, rubric-judgement-result, draftFingerprint, scoringMethod: judgement, Choice map, Score criteria\\n\\n## Task 3: Add optional read-only writing lenses, partial\\n\\n### rollout_summary_files\\n\\n- rollout_summaries/REDACTED.md (cwd=/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne, rollout_path=/home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00, thread_id=01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385, partial; UI checks deferred to user)\\n\\n### keywords\\n\\n- writing-lenses, WRITING_LENSES, reader, revision, voice, promises, scraps, room, circling, research, writing-tools-storage, stale-result\\n\\n## User preferences\\n\\n- when hosted TypeSafe/Jev integration was discussed, the user said it \\\"should work through notorganic in actuality rather than tied through this deployment directly\\\" and wanted an API \\\"that just works with jev\\\" -> place provider credentials, authorization, customer inspection, and ledger accounting behind Not Organic. [Task 1]\\n- when dirty provider files were deliberately left alone, the user asked to \\\"finish the application\\\" -> complete the requested product side with guarded/narrow patches while preserving unrelated in-flight provider work. [Task 1]\\n- when implementation was requested, the user said \\\"don't manual test things here ... don't bother with tests either pure implementation\\\" -> stop tests and browser/manual UI checks at that explicit boundary and report the resulting verification gap plainly. [Task 2][Task 3]\\n\\n## Reusable knowledge\\n\\n- Production Twyne calls Not Organic using DPoP and `judgement:evaluate` at `POST /v1/judgement`; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is only loopback/local fallback. The provider owns the key, typed state/questions transport, model alias resolution, and per-account reserve -> dispatch -> accept -> settle/reconcile accounting. [Task 1]\\n- Jev question types are `noul`, `choice`, and `score`; normalize Twyne arrays into TypeSafe Choice maps, retain Score ordered arrays, bound requests, avoid upstream response bodies that may echo documents, and surface uncertain/missing usage rather than silently billing zero. The observed rate was `0.042` microUSD per input token. [Task 1]\\n- `runRubricPass()` batches enabled criteria and degrades safely; `judgementRubricResult()` rejects incomplete criteria and protects saves with folio/brief/criteria/draft fingerprint freshness guards. Confidence is distribution concentration, not truth or permission to act. [Task 2]\\n- The eight read-only lenses (`reader`, `revision`, `voice`, `promises`, `scraps`, `room`, `circling`, `research`) live in `src/utils/writing-lenses.ts`, with UI/storage at `src/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx` and `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`. Quote supplied passages, bound inputs, expose missing evidence/uncertainty, reject stale results, and never edit prose automatically. [Task 3]\\n\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\n\\n- Source edits, a configured gateway variable, and a later successful Railway status call are not deployment/live-route/ledger proof. Final state was uncommitted and undeployed, with no final typecheck, tests, browser checks, or live request after the last edits. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\\n- Broken Python `PYTHONHOME`/`PYTHONPATH` -> use `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH python3 ...` for required scripts. GitNexus `UNKNOWN` from wrong symbols -> resolve the exact symbol (`createGateway`) before treating impact output as evidence. [Task 1]\\n\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1d6dda\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004171,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2628,\"output\":\"<!-- convex-ai-start -->\\nThis project uses [Convex](https://convex.dev) as its backend.\\n\\nWhen working on Convex code, **always read `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` first** for important guidelines on how to correctly use Convex APIs and patterns. The file contains rules that override what you may have learned about Convex from training data.\\n\\nConvex agent skills for common tasks can be installed by running `npx convex ai-files install`.\\n<!-- convex-ai-end -->\\n---\\nname: typesafe-ai\\nlicense: MIT\\ndescription: >\\n  Build AI-powered software with TypeSafe: small units of AI intelligence you\\n  can use like programming primitives. Its System One models, including Jev,\\n  turn natural language and application state into typed judgments and\\n  probabilities that code can combine. Use when a feature needs programmable\\n  common sense, when brainstorming what AI could make possible in an app, or\\n  when an LLM prompt-and-parse step could become a structured decision.\\n  Applications include routing, ranking, extraction, verification, and\\n  interactive experiences; these are starting points, not the limits.\\n  Read live docs and cookbooks to find useful patterns and discover new combinations.\\n---\\n\\n# Build with TypeSafe\\n\\nTypeSafe makes units of AI intelligence usable like programming primitives: small\\njudgments you can compose into larger capabilities. Its **System One models** return\\nfast, focused judgments that software can consume directly. **Jev** is TypeSafe's\\nflagship and first System One model. It understands natural language and returns\\ntyped answers and probabilities rather\\nthan generating text or reasoning explanations. Code owns the workflow; the model\\nsupplies programmable common sense where ordinary code needs semantic understanding.\\n\\n## Read the live docs\\n\\n**The live TypeSafe docs are the source of truth. Read them as part of the task.**\\nThis skill gives direction; the docs carry current concepts, prompting guidance,\\nAPI contracts, SDK usage, models, limits, and worked examples.\\n\\n- Start with the [documentation index](https://docs.typesafe.ai/llms.txt) to discover\\n  relevant pages and cookbooks. Use targeted reads rather than loading the entire site.\\n- Mintlify serves Markdown by appending `.md` to a page path, for example\\n  [how to build with TypeSafe](https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/how-to-build-with-system-one.md).\\n  Follow links from the index; convert extensionless documentation page links to\\n  `.md` when useful. Resolve relative links against `https://docs.typesafe.ai`.\\n- Before writing an integration, read the current API or chosen SDK page and the\\n  question guidance relevant to the design. For a new workflow, also inspect the\\n  closest cookbook: it often shows a better decomposition than a generic classifier.\\n- If the index is unavailable, use the direct links below or the site's navigation.\\n  If Markdown fetching fails, try the normal page. If live access is unavailable,\\n  use available local docs or installed SDK types, state that limitation, and avoid\\n  inventing version-dependent details.\\n\\n| Task | Start here; follow the relevant details |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Understand the programming model | [System One](https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/system-one.md), [building guide](https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/how-to-build-with-system-one.md) |\\n| Explore what to build | [Use-case map](https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/use-case-map.md), then relevant cookbooks from the index |\\n| Prepare inputs and questions | [State](https://docs.typesafe.ai/concepts/state.md), [primitives](https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives.md), then the chosen primitive's page |\\n| Decide how to handle uncertainty | [Confidence](https://docs.typesafe.ai/confidence.md) |\\n| Write API code | [HTTP API](https://docs.typesafe.ai/api.md), [Python SDK](https://docs.typesafe.ai/sdk/python.md), or [JavaScript SDK](https://docs.typesafe.ai/sdk/javascript.md) |\\n| Update an older integration | [Migration guide](https://docs.typesafe.ai/migrating-to-v1.md) and the installed SDK's current reference |\\n\\n## Find the useful shape\\n\\nStart from the behavior the user wants: what will the application show, select,\\nchange, or hand off? Work backward to the judgments it needs. Keep known rules,\\ncalculations, exact lookups, and execution in code. Preserve the user's chosen stack\\nand scope; add TypeSafe where semantic understanding helps.\\n\\nWhen brainstorming or choosing an architecture, consider more than classification.\\nThe patterns below are starting points: combine primitives around the user's goal,\\nincluding ideas that do not fit an established recipe.\\n\\n- **Route and fill known arguments.** A request can select a handler and its typed\\n  parameters. Ask useful branch-specific questions up front and consume only the\\n  relevant answers. Explore [function calling](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/function_calling.md)\\n  and [speculative fan-out](https://docs.typesafe.ai/patterns/fan-out.md).\\n- **Select instead of generate.** Find candidate values or source spans in code,\\n  use a judgment to select the intended one, then copy or normalize it. Code can\\n  also assemble source text into a formatted document or reading guide. Explore\\n  [value extraction](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/pre_parsed_value_extraction_cookbook.md)\\n  and [structure recovery](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/autoformat.md).\\n- **Find and judge evidence.** Retrieve candidates, compare their relevance to a\\n  query, and select useful context. Explore [reranking](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/rerank_typesafe.md)\\n  and [hierarchical classification](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/hierarchical_classification.md).\\n- **Turn judgments into reusable data.** Score dimensions once, then let code or\\n  user controls change weights, thresholds, rankings, and views. With labeled\\n  outcomes, those signals can become classical ML features. Explore\\n  [composite scoring](https://docs.typesafe.ai/patterns/composite-scoring.md) and\\n  [feature discovery](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/autoresearch_feature_discovery.md).\\n- **Verify and escalate.** Check specific claims or fields against their evidence;\\n  send uncertain or failing cases to a person or reasoning model. Explore\\n  [citation checks](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/citation_check.md) and\\n  [extraction cascades](https://docs.typesafe.ai/cookbooks/sde_cascade.md).\\n- **Respond to changing state.** Code can retain goals and observations while fresh\\n  judgments guide the next bounded step. Keep inferred state distinct from observed\\n  facts, and check freshness before applying a result to a changed situation.\\n\\nFor open-ended requests, offer the few directions that best serve the user's goal\\nand recommend a starting point. For a concrete request, choose the relevant pattern\\nand build; a brainstorm is not a mandatory detour.\\n\\n## Design the judgments\\n\\nChoose by what the answer means, then read the relevant primitive page:\\n\\n| Need | Primitive | Important distinction |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| One of a defined set | [Choice](https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/choice.md) | Picks one option; its distribution compares competing options |\\n| Whether a condition holds | [Noul](https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/noul.md) | Probability of yes; no separate confidence; use one per label when several may apply |\\n| Degree along a described dimension | [Score](https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/score.md) | Probability-weighted position on ordered levels; use comparable per-item Scores for graded ranking |\\n\\nGive each question enough relevant **state** to answer: source text, identities,\\nrelationships, policies, and current facts. Prefer named JSON fields when context\\nhas several parts. Put the judgment in **instructions** and define its possible\\nanswers in **criteria**. Question IDs are for code and are not sent to the model;\\ninclude complete meaning in the question. Reference nested state with backticked\\npaths such as `ticket.messages[0].text`.\\n\\nAsk one narrow, coherent judgment per question. Split independently useful dimensions,\\nwithout destroying the relationship being judged. A bounded action selection or\\ncontextual interpretation is valid; atomic does not mean literal fact extraction\\nor a one-sentence limit. Strings work for simple questions. Use structured objects\\nor arrays when definitions, contrasts, exclusions, or examples clarify instructions\\nor criteria. Score levels must describe concrete situations and stand on their own.\\n\\nKeep the needed answers available. Include a no-match outcome when nothing may fit;\\nuse a separate presence judgment when it is independently useful. For source-value\\nselection, check candidate coverage: the model cannot choose an omitted value.\\n\\n## Compose and verify\\n\\n**Ask independent questions over the same state together**, including useful\\nspeculative questions. They run in parallel and cannot see one another's answers.\\nState each speculative premise explicitly; code consumes the applicable answers.\\nA second request is warranted when an earlier answer is needed to fetch evidence,\\nconstruct new state, or determine the next options. Extra questions still use tokens;\\nmeasure actual request budgets, cost, and end-to-end latency.\\n\\nUse probabilities and confidence to guide behavior, with thresholds evaluated on\\nthe user's data and consequences. Choice/Score confidence summarizes distribution\\nconcentration, not overall workflow correctness or permission to act. A Noul near\\n0.5 means similar probability for yes and no, not medium intensity. Several\\nacceptable alternatives can also spread probability; low confidence need not\\ninvalidate a harmless preference choice. Ignore uncertainty on unused branches.\\n\\nKeep policy explicit and raw judgments reusable. Weighted scores suit compensating\\npreferences; an “any serious violation” rule needs separate conditions. Changing a\\nweight or display filter need not rerun inference when evidence and question meanings\\nare unchanged. Typed output guarantees the interface, not truth. System One models\\nare trained for calibrated decisions; validate their performance in the target domain.\\n\\nTest representative cases and the resulting application behavior. For failures,\\ninspect the exact state, questions, candidates, answers, composition, and observed\\noutcome. Separate missing evidence, model errors, code errors, and service failures.\\nTreat cookbook thresholds and demo results as examples to evaluate, not universal\\nrules or permanent model limitations. Keep API credentials server-side in web apps.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"70273a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007265,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":937,\"output\":\" M convex/_generated/api.d.ts\\n M convex/agentPrompts.ts\\n M convex/agents.ts\\n M convex/lib/rateLimit.ts\\n M convex/providerIdentity.ts\\n M devenv.lock\\n M prompts/custom-criterion-user.md\\n M prompts/dossier-check-system.md\\n M prompts/dossier-check-user.md\\n M prompts/evidence-judge-user.md\\n M prompts/integrity-judge-user.md\\n M prompts/missing-source-detector-user.md\\n M prompts/sufficiency-judge-user.md\\n M prompts/target-fit-judge-system.md\\n M prompts/target-fit-judge-user.md\\n M skills-lock.json\\n M src/components/editor/insert-panels.tsx\\n M src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx\\n M src/components/editor/math/math-source-editor.ts\\n M src/components/editor/math/math.css\\n M src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx\\n M src/components/landing/landing-page.tsx\\n M src/components/landing/workspace-preview.tsx\\n M src/components/rubric/rubric-panel.tsx\\n M src/components/ui/text-modal.stories.tsx\\n M src/components/ui/text-modal.tsx\\n M src/global.css\\n M src/routes/download/[platform]/index.ts\\n M src/routes/downloads/index.tsx\\n M src/routes/editor/index.tsx\\n M src/routes/pricing/index.tsx\\n M src/routes/rubric/index.tsx\\n M src/routes/settings/index.tsx\\n M src/types/index.ts\\n M src/utils/feature-flags.ts\\n M src/utils/icon-system.ts\\n M src/utils/idb.ts\\n M src/utils/notorganic-provider.ts\\n M src/utils