{"timestamp":"2026-09-20T06:04:06.779Z","ordinal":106,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0bd6a-2afb-7801-81a8-f98a3130643b","call_id":"call_UM6sR8LKtjrK2n3LG7Mmnyzc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 11420)\nTotal output lines: 4\n\n{\"i\":0,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"cf4be2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004491,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3532,\"output\":\"thread_id: 01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385\\nupdated_at: 2026-09-18T23:58:45+00:00\\nrollout_path: /home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/18/rollout-2026-09-18T19-43-22-01a0b6e7-3c95-7543-9f88-4698f314c385.jsonl\\ncwd: /home/diogenes/Projects/twyne\\ngit_branch: main\\n\\n# Twyne Jev integration and writing tools implementation\\n\\nRollout context: In `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne`, the user asked to finish the Not Organic-backed Jev integration, wire Jev-first rubric scoring, and add eight optional writing-analysis tools. The provider repo was `/home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider`. The user explicitly stopped manual UI checks and tests: “don't manual test things here ... don't bother with tests either pure implementation.”\\n\\n## Task 1: Jev provider and gateway integration\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nPreference signals:\\n\\n- The user asked to “finish the application” after deliberately staging provider edits rather than touching dirty files, indicating they value completing the integration while preserving unrelated in-flight provider work.\\n- The user explicitly requested pure implementation and asked the agent not to run tests or manual UI checks; future similar work should stop verification at the user’s boundary unless they later request it.\\n\\nKey steps:\\n\\n- Inspected existing `convex/systemOne.ts`, `src/utils/system-one.ts`, and the staged provider installation document.\\n- Installed provider-side Jev configuration, route registration, and capability support in the Not Organic repo using guarded file-hash application scripts.\\n- Added/updated `JudgementGateway`, `GatewayConfig.typesafe`, `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`/`TYPESAFE_MODEL` configuration, `/v1/judgement`, model advertisement, and `judgement:evaluate` capability.\\n- Normalized Twyne’s array criteria into TypeSafe’s documented Choice map shape and added request/response validation, limits, stale-response handling, timeout behavior, idempotency replay handling, and conservative reconciliation for unknown usage/delivery.\\n- Configured the gateway’s `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` from the existing Skate secret with automatic deployment disabled. This was reported successful, but deployment/live endpoint verification was not performed.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n\\n- Initial live Railway status access failed due temporary DNS/OAuth network errors; a later status call succeeded. Do not treat source changes or variable configuration as deployment proof.\\n- A first provider patch attempt failed because the local Python runtime had a broken `PYTHONHOME`; rerunning with `env -u PYTHONHOME -u PYTHONPATH` worked.\\n- GitNexus lookups for incorrect symbol names returned `UNKNOWN`; the correct gateway symbol was `createGateway`. Resolve exact symbols before relying on impact output.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n\\n- Twyne production prefers Not Organic whenever enabled; direct `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` is intended only for loopback/local development. Not Organic owns the provider key, capability authorization, per-account ledger reservation/settlement, and Jev model alias resolution.\\n- The provider route is `POST /v1/judgement`, authenticated with the existing DPoP product boundary and capability `judgement:evaluate`; products send typed `state` and `questions`, not chat prompts.\\n- Jev uses three question types: `noul`, `choice`, and `score`. TypeSafe Choice criteria are maps; Score criteria are ordered arrays. Independent questions over shared state can be batched.\\n- Provider accounting reserves before upstream, marks dispatch/acceptance, settles using reported `input_tokens` at `0.042` microUSD/token, and reconciles missing usage or uncertain delivery rather than silently billing zero.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- Twyne files: `convex/systemOne.ts`, `convex/lib/judgementContract.ts`, `src/utils/system-one.ts`, `src/utils/rubric-grade.ts`.\\n- Provider files: `apps/gateway/src/judgement.ts`, `apps/gateway/src/app.ts`, `apps/gateway/src/main.ts`, `apps/gateway/src/types.ts`, `packages/contracts/src/catalog.ts`.\\n- Route: `POST /v1/judgement`; capability: `judgement:evaluate`; gateway env: `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`, optional `TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-latest`.\\n- Final implementation state was explicitly reported as uncommitted and undeployed; no live request or ledger verification was completed.\\n\\n## Task 2: Jev-first rubric scoring\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nKey steps:\\n\\n- Added a Jev-first rubric pass using one batched request for enabled criteria, with frontier/persona fallback when Jev is unavailable.\\n- Added cached probabilities, model provenance, distributions, custom-criteria support, writer-weight recalculation, draft/folio/brief freshness guards, and a `draftFingerprint`.\\n- Updated rubric reporting to distinguish typed model judgements from editorial/persona readings and to flag uncertain distributions for a second opinion.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n\\n- `runRubricPass()` in `src/utils/rubric-grade.ts` is the transport seam; it returns a result and degrades rather than throwing.\\n- `judgementRubricResult()` in `src/utils/rubric-judgement-result.ts` converts typed Jev marks into UI-compatible rubric results and rejects incomplete answers.\\n- Jev confidence describes distribution concentration, not truth or permission to act; bimodal/uncertain score distributions should be surfaced rather than treated as definitive.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- `src/components/rubric/rubric-panel.tsx`\\n- `src/routes/rubric/index.tsx`\\n- `src/utils/rubric-judgement-result.ts`\\n- `src/types/index.ts`\\n\\n## Task 3: Eight optional writing tools\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nKey steps:\\n\\n- Added eight selectable lenses under `/writing-tools/`: reader-without-ending, revision cost, voice preservation, reader promises, scraps reuse, editorial disagreement, revision circling, and research drift.\\n- Added folio-scoped local notebook storage for audience, voice examples, scraps, claims/sources, and intentional unresolved promises.\\n- Added evidence quoting, bounded inputs, explicit missing-input states, uncertainty notices, stale-result rejection, and protection against checking outdated claim wording.\\n- Added an editor navigation link labeled “Writing tools”.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n\\n- Core logic is in `src/utils/writing-lenses.ts`; UI is `src/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx`; storage is `src/utils/writing-tools-storage.ts`; route is `src/routes/writing-tools/index.tsx`.\\n- The lenses are read-only: Jev classifies supplied evidence and does not generate prose or edit the draft.\\n- Research drift checks only explicitly supplied claim/source pairs and prevents rechecking when the saved claim no longer matches the current draft.\\n- Intentional promises are excluded by stable IDs generated with `promiseId()`.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- `WRITING_LENSES` and `runWritingLens()` in `src/utils/writing-lenses.ts`.\\n- Editor link added in `src/routes/editor/index.tsx`.\\n- User-facing route: `/writing-tools/`.\\n\\n## Verification status\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\n- Before the user’s stop instruction, the rollout reported 60 targeted tests for rubric integration and 1104 Twyne tests from earlier work, but the final implementation was not re-tested afterward.\\n- Prettier was run on selected Twyne files.\\n- No final typecheck, test suite, browser/UI check, deployment, or live gateway/ledger verification was run after the final edits.\\n- Changes remained uncommitted and undeployed.\\nthread_id: 01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4\\nupdated_at: 2026-09-19T12:41:05+00:00\\nrollout_path: /home/diogenes/.codex/sessions/2026/09/19/rollout-2026-09-19T08-03-45-01a0b98d-1310-7722-85ad-98bdd317bee4.jsonl\\ncwd: /home/diogenes/Projects/keating\\ngit_branch: chore/android-gradle-heap-fix\\n\\n# Jev/model-cascade integration advanced from plan into a shared judgement foundation, but the overall plan remains incomplete\\n\\nRollout context: `/home/diogenes/Projects/keating`, branch `chore/android-gradle-heap-fix`. The user’s active objective was to finish `docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md` end to end. Existing worktree was already heavily modified; only newly relevant files are summarized below.\\n\\n## Task 1: Shared judgement contracts and cascade foundation\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nPreference signals:\\n\\n- The user explicitly requested “do it all end to end,” “Full replacement everywhere,” and a separately configurable local judgement model; future work should preserve the full scope rather than stop at a contract-only slice.\\n\\nKey steps:\\n\\n- Added `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/` with contracts, projections, router, wire codec, hosted System One caller, local backend, assessment helpers, retrieval helpers, and boosting helpers.\\n- Exported the new API through `packages/learner-contracts/src/index.ts`.\\n- Added extensive tests for primitives, routing, backends, assessment decisions, retrieval, and boosting.\\n- Added `web/src/keating/judgement-model.ts` and a separate local setting defaulting to `RASMUS/MiniCPM5-2B-ONNX`, with `off|local|hosted` backend preference and same-origin gateway validation.\\n- Verified package tests reached `187 pass / 0 fail` across 16 files and package typecheck passed after fixing an incorrect type import.\\n- Verified the judgement-model setting test after adding the repository’s localStorage/window test shim: `10 pass / 0 fail`.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n\\n- The shared package is the correct location for router/contracts because CLI, web, and mobile already import `@keating/learner-contracts`; putting the router only under `src/` would prevent cross-platform reuse.\\n- `JudgementProvenance.source` is literally `\\\"proxy\\\"`; thresholds are keyed by backend/model/calibration/question digest; router pinning prevents fallback during evolution experiments.\\n- Hosted System One transport preserves protocol asymmetries: Choice criteria map, Score criteria ordered array, Noul has no confidence. Credentials are optional and omitted for same-origin gateway use.\\n- Local judgement returns typed closed-vocabulary answers from Needle/local-model label scores and omits unanswerable questions rather than guessing.\\n- Assessment helpers enforce one-directional readiness Nouls, per-item performance Nouls, bucketed duration/due-date Choices, modal-level Score interpretation, and pending grading on uncertainty.\\n- Retrieval helpers enforce centered/z-score similarity rather than raw cosine, deterministic shortlist fallback, exact learner-message evidence, observed confidence ≤0.65, and a 128-fact cap.\\n- Boosting helpers fit a depth-limited decision tree before more complex boosting and evaluate only deterministic held-out rows.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n\\n- Initial web setting tests failed because Bun’s test environment had no `localStorage`; follow existing tests by installing an inline storage/window/custom-event shim.\\n- Initial package typecheck failed because assessment types were imported from `projections.ts` instead of `contracts.ts`; Bun tests did not catch this because type-only imports were stripped. Always run TypeScript after Bun tests.\\n- The boosting implementation and tests were added but were not yet fully reverified in the captured rollout after addition; do not claim the complete package remained green without rerunning.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/contracts.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/projections.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/router.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/wire.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/system-one.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/local-backend.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/assessment.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/retrieval.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/src/judgement/boosting.ts`\\n- `web/src/keating/judgement-model.ts`\\n- `packages/learner-contracts/test/judgement*.test.ts`\\n- `web/src/test/judgement-model-setting.test.ts`\\n- Verified command: `cd packages/learner-contracts && bun test` → `187 pass / 0 fail`; `bun run typecheck` passed before later boosting additions.\\n\\n## Task 2: Planned replacement of judge sites and remaining phases\\n\\nOutcome: partial\\n\\nKey steps:\\n\\n- Spawned workers for benchmark judge replacement, web export/trajectory judge replacement, and CLI/evolution judge replacement.\\n- All three workers terminated with usage-limit errors before delivering implementation.\\n- Consequently, the major planned integrations remain incomplete: `scripts/training/benchmark_judge.py`, `web/src/keating/export-judge.ts`, `web/src/keating/trajectory-passes.ts`, `shared/evolution/model-adapters.ts`, CLI mastery/profile/policy integration, telemetry, and end-to-end wiring.\\n\\nFailures and how to do differently:\\n\\n- Do not treat the shared contract layer as completion of `docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md`; the plan explicitly requires all judge-site replacements, benchmark A/B harness, telemetry, evolution pinning, and verification.\\n- Re-run the full package and web/root checks after every subsequent change. Required web sequence is `cd web && bun run panda`, then `bunx tsc --noEmit`, then `bun test`.\\n- Worker failure was resource-related, not a code diagnosis; continue implementation directly or use smaller scoped tasks rather than assuming worker changes landed.\\n\\nReusable knowledge:\\n\\n- The authoritative in-repo plan is `docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md` (35.9 KB, created during this rollout).\\n- The worktree is heavily dirty with many unrelated pre-existing modifications; inspect targeted diffs carefully and avoid reverting unrelated changes.\\n- Existing plan constraints include server-side-only TypeSafe credentials, `NEEDLE_TELEMETRY=0` and `DO_NOT_TRACK=1`, no upstream error-body exposure, evidence taxonomy preservation, and no automatic irreversible action from judgement alone.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- `docs/plans/jev-model-cascade.md`\\n- Existing worker assignments targeted:\\n  - `scripts/training/benchmark_judge.py`\\n  - `web/src/keating/export-judge.ts`\\n  - `web/src/keating/trajectory-passes.ts`\\n  - `shared/evolution/model-adapters.ts`\\n  - `src/core/policy-judgement.ts`\\n  - `src/core/mastery.ts`\\n  - `src/core/learner-state.ts`\\n- Worker notifications: all three reported usage-limit errors; no implementation result was delivered.\\n\"}}\n{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"32b7f3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008966,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3519,\"output\":\"src/components/editor/manuscript-panel.tsx:207:          <LastSavedLine savedAt={store.lastSavedAt} /> ·{\\\" \\\"}\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:20:  emptyWritingToolsNotebook,\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:21:  loadWritingToolsNotebook,\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:22:  saveWritingToolsNotebook,\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:23:  type WritingToolsNotebook,\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:40:  notebook: WritingToolsNotebook;\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:51:  saveNotice: string;\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:114:function materialPreview(state: ToolsState): string {\\nsrc/components/writing-tools/writing-tools.tsx:136:export const 