{"timestamp":"2026-09-20T07:16:44.496Z","ordinal":1065,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0bd62-eabf-7a61-bb50-27a4047f7c4a","turn_id":"01a0bd95-790e-7882-b1b0-52e1002bd152","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-daf928b6-47d9-40bb-b1ab-6866bf4d64f1","process_id":"55063","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rtk proxy cat apps/gateway/src/judgement.INSTALL.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/diogenes/Projects/notorganic-provider","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rtk proxy cat apps/gateway/src/judgement.INSTALL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Judgement gateway integration\n\nInstalled in `types.ts`, `main.ts`, `app.ts`, and the capability catalog.\nThe authenticated `POST /v1/judgement` route requires `judgement:evaluate`.\n`GET /v1/models` advertises `judgement` only when the gateway has a TypeSafe key.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` on the gateway service only. `TYPESAFE_MODEL` is optional\nand defaults to `jev-latest`. Products use the `judgement` alias; the gateway\nowns the upstream version. Twyne prefers Not Organic whenever enabled and\naccepts a direct key only in a loopback Convex runtime.\n\n## Requests and accounting\n\nSend a string or object of strings in `state` and a map of typed `questions`.\nChoice criteria accept the documented map or Twyne's internal array of labels;\narrays are normalized before calling TypeSafe. Scores retain ordered arrays.\nRequests are bounded by context, question count, and the caller's credit cap.\n\nAn optional idempotency key (1–255 characters) enables replay of a settled\nresponse without another upstream request or charge. Omitting the key starts\na new evaluation. In-flight duplicates return 409. Settlement uses reported\ninput tokens at 0.042 microUSD per token; output is free. Responses are stored\nthrough the existing encrypted response ledger. Unknown delivery or missing\nusage enters reconciliation instead of pretending the call cost nothing.\n\n## Delivery status\n\nThe route and product UI are implemented locally. Deployment and live\naccount-to-ledger verification are separate from these source changes.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Judgement gateway integration\n\nInstalled in `types.ts`, `main.ts`, `app.ts`, and the capability catalog.\nThe authenticated `POST /v1/judgement` route requires `judgement:evaluate`.\n`GET /v1/models` advertises `judgement` only when the gateway has a TypeSafe key.\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` on the gateway service only. `TYPESAFE_MODEL` is optional\nand defaults to `jev-latest`. Products use the `judgement` alias; the gateway\nowns the upstream version. Twyne prefers Not Organic whenever enabled and\naccepts a direct key only in a loopback Convex runtime.\n\n## Requests and accounting\n\nSend a string or object of strings in `state` and a map of typed `questions`.\nChoice criteria accept the documented map or Twyne's internal array of labels;\narrays are normalized before calling TypeSafe. Scores retain ordered arrays.\nRequests are bounded by context, question count, and the caller's credit cap.\n\nAn optional idempotency key (1–255 characters) enables replay of a settled\nresponse without another upstream request or charge. Omitting the key starts\na new evaluation. In-flight duplicates return 409. Settlement uses reported\ninput tokens at 0.042 microUSD per token; output is free. Responses are stored\nthrough the existing encrypted response ledger. Unknown delivery or missing\nusage enters reconciliation instead of pretending the call cost nothing.\n\n## Delivery status\n\nThe route and product UI are implemented locally. Deployment and live\naccount-to-ledger verification are separate from these source changes.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":674278510},"formatted_output":"# Judgement gateway integration\n\nInstalled in `types.ts`, `main.ts`, `app.ts`, and the capability catalog.\nThe authenticated `POST /v1/judgement`